        "original_id": "b2393781-25af-5bad-96a7-7baa0bea3178",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sandy Fox, Tiggy, Mike Judge, Greg Daniels, Judy and Mary\n- Works: King of the Hill, Freckles, Sobakasu, Rurouni Kenshin, Why\n- Roles: voice actress, singer, dancer\n- Topics: animated cartoons, anime, video games, American animated sitcoms, Southeast Asia\n\nFacts:\n- Sandra Marie Fox was born on July 13, 1963.\n- Sandy Fox is an American voice actress, singer, and dancer.\n- Sandy Fox has had numerous roles in animated cartoons, anime, and video games.\n- King of the Hill is an American animated sitcom created by Mike Judge and Greg Daniels.\n- King of the Hill aired on Fox from January 12, 1997 to September 13, 2009.\n- Tiggy is perhaps best known for her remix of Sandy Fox's song \"Freckles\".\n- \"Freckles\" was originally the English version of \"Sobakasu\" by Judy and Mary from the anime Rurouni Kenshin.\n- Tiggy is also popular in parts of Southeast Asia with the song \"Why\".",
